# Medical Research Assistant (Private Health Sector):  A toolkit for health=
care professionals conducting research in private settings. Features  data =
collection tools, analysis scripts, and regulatory documentation templates.=
 Streamlines clinical research workflows while maintaining healthcare compl=
iance and data security standards.
This is Web application written in Flask,=20
featuring a Medical Assistant Chatbot powered by=20
Large Language Models (LLMs) and Retrieval Augmented Generation (RAG).
It uses <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 te=
xt-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]=
">langchain</code> as underlying library, leveraging <code class=3D"bg-text=
-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-w=
rap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">langchain</code>'s <code cla=
ss=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whi=
tespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">agents</code> a=
nd <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-da=
nger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">too=
ls</code>=20
to build a RAG system that can use tools such as vector stores and SQL data=
bases.=20
The underlying LLM is <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border=
-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px=
 text-[0.9rem]">llama3.1</code> provided by <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 bo=
rder border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap round=
ed-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">ollama</code>. <code class=3D"bg-text=
-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-w=
rap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">SQLite</code> is used as und=
erlying=20
database and <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 border-border-3=
00 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.=
9rem]">FAISS</code> as vector store.
Each of these technologies runs locally, and no API keys are required.
## Disclaimer
This is just a toy project, and the outputs of the Medical Assistant=20
should not be considered as medical advice in any way.
## Features
- The user can interact with the Medical Assistant via a chat.
The Medical Assistant can provide useful feedback to the user's questions,
also leveraging additional datasets as knowledge-base with RAG.=20
- The system maintains a database of patients, doctors, appointments, and c=
hat history.
- The Medical Assistant can suggest an appointment with a suitable doctor,=
=20
based on the user's questions.=20
- The Medical Assistant can show available slots for appointments,
and the user can reserve an appointment, view and modify its appointments.
- The user can download their chat history.
- The user can report a health emergency, which is going to be registered b=
y the Assistant=20
together with a color code (RED, GREEN, YELLOW) for immediate consultation =
by healthcare=20
professionals (using the <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 bor=
der-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py=
-px text-[0.9rem]">src/check_emergencies.py</code> script).
## Requirements
- Python 3.10
- Install requirements: <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border border-0.5 bord=
er-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4rem] px-1 py-=
px text-[0.9rem]">pip install -r requirements.txt</code>
- Install [Ollama](<a href=3D"https://ollama.com/download">https://ollama.c=
om/download</a>)
- At least 8GB RAM
- Nvidia GPU with at least 2GB dedicated memory
## Setup
1. Data is in data folder.
2. Preparation of vector index: run <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border bor=
der-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0.4r=
em] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">src/create_index.py</code>.
3. Preparation of SQLite database: run <code class=3D"bg-text-200/5 border =
border-0.5 border-border-300 text-danger-000 whitespace-pre-wrap rounded-[0=
.4rem] px-1 py-px text-[0.9rem]">src/create_db.py</code>
